Hi all,

On Friday, Per joined me online and we worked on a number of updates:

The Renin website is now on GitHub and ready for pull requests:
https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin-website

The package database is (packages.renjin.org <http://packages.renjin.org>) is also on GitHub now:
https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin-packages

We improved the search function and added a contribution form  <https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin-webapp/commit/2e2ab2aeb3049f39e83a40839544d33a62103604>for packages developed exclusively for renjin and published to Maven Central, like Per's spreadsheet <https://packages.renjin.org/package/se.alipsa/spreadsheets> package.
https://packages.renjin.org/packages/contribute

We also prepared for the Renjin 3.5.0 release. All of the packages on our "must pass" list were passing <https://build.renjin.org/job/Renjin-Release/25/> (1 is now broken?). I hope we can do the final 3.5.0 release during our next working session, which I'd like to schedule for July 30th.

Renjin Working Session
Friday, July 30 · 15:00 – 19:00 (Amsterdam)
Google Meet joining info
Video call link: https://meet.google.com/iid-wsxn-qeb

Thanks again!

Alex

--
